X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/workshop-platen-press-fundamentals/", "Creative Sonoma": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/workshop-platen-press-fundamentals/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/workshop-platen-press-fundamentals/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Workshop: Platen Press Fundamentals
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T150000
UID:260713Qn7Qf-qpDkeVVLMze5-O0Q
DESCRIPTION:PLATEN PRESS FUNDAMENTALS Master the platen press by designing
  and printing your own edition of letterpress greeting cards. This worksho
 p focuses on the specific techniques and rhythm of platen press operation-
 feeding paper\, achieving even impression\, and producing clean\, consiste
 nt prints. You'll set metal type to create one card design\, then print an
  edition of 15 cards to take home. Through hands-on practice\, you'll lear
 n makeready\, lockup\, ink coverage\, and troubleshooting common press iss
 ues. By the end of the workshop\, you'll understand how to operate a plate
 n press confidently and have beautiful cards ready to send or gift. Ideal 
 for printers who want to add platen press skills to their repertoire and c
 reate functional\, finished work. third saturdays\\* 10:00am - 3:00pm \\*n
 o class in November
LOCATION:D
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/workshop-platen-press-fundamentals/
X-SOURCE:Creative Sonoma, North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://napavalleymuseum.org/blogs/upcoming-exhibitions/eames-eames"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T170000
UID:2610044WraOXTwikCNVBl901Wqjg
DESCRIPTION:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design\n\nCr
 eated in collaboration with the Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.\n\n
 EAMES & EAMES explores the iterative\, hands-on\, and human-centered appr
 oach of Charles & Ray Eames. Through furniture\, toys\, paintings\, graphi
 cs\, and personal belongings collected over their lifetimes\, this groundb
 reaking exhibition looks beyond the iconic Eames chairs to reveal the brea
 dth of their creative practice. More than any single object\, their work o
 pened doors to new and unexpected ways of seeing\, thinking\, making\, and
  understanding the world—ideas that continue to inspire us today.\n\nCur
 ated by Llisa Demetrios\, Co-Founder & The Lucia Eames Chief Curator of th
 e Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.
LOCATION:The MAC - Napa Valley Museum of Art & Culture
URL:https://napavalleymuseum.org/blogs/upcoming-exhibitions/eames-eames
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
