BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/109114546?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:S.R. Laws
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T170000
UID:261111vLR74WDcMkaNm0nY9KscBg
DESCRIPTION:S.R. LAWS IS OUT THERE: He approaches songwriting with a passi
 on for songs that we all grew up on. His sound rings a familiar bell in yo
 ur head while still delivering ideas completely unique.  He draws inspirat
 ion from outstanding storytellers like John Hiatt\, Lucinda Williams\, Rod
 ney Crowell\, Steve Earle\, Neil Finn\, Patty Griffin\, Chuck Prophet\, an
 d Ron Sexsmith. All of their music and others have carved a deep groove. \
 n\nGrowing up out there in Northern California\, he developed a unique con
 nection to music early on. His father worked as a trash collector\, and he
  would spend hours sifting through bags of discarded 45 records. Each find
  felt like stumbling upon hidden treasures. Some records were covered in d
 irt and grime\, while others were pristine. The thrill of discovering new 
 sounds was exhilarating\, and he could hardly wait to drop the needle and 
 immerse himself in the music.\n\nHe embarked on a pilgrimage to Texas with
  just two suitcases and $500 in his bank account. His goal was to dive int
 o the vibrant music scene and learn from fellow songwriters. Austin\, know
 n as the "Live Music Capital of the World\," offered countless opportuniti
 es for him to grow as an artist. Open mics and songwriters' nights became 
 his training ground\, where he soaked up every moment\, listening to other
 s share their stories through music.\n\nThese days\, he resides in Sonoma 
 County\, California\, working hard as a touring artist and singer-songwrit
 er for his original rock band\, The Heartsleeves. He invites everyone to j
 oin him on this musical journey\, sharing his songs one person at a time i
 n this vast and unpredictable world we live in.\n\nA.M. Sessions \n\nCheck
  out the latest album from S.R. Laws-  "A.M. Sessions." It's a collection 
 of songs that I am incredibly proud of\, crafted with the help of old frie
 nds and intrepid new collaborators. I can tell you more about it sometime.
  Come out and grab a copy at one of the shows or you can find it online. 
 “\n\n“ It is through forthright lyrics that are personal and earnest\,
  that he \\(Laws\\) composes lyrical pictures. Taking snapshots from the m
 ost common walks of life filtered through his own joy and tribulations.”
   - David Sampson - Producer Studio Secti West\n\n“..relaxed mid-tempo A
 mericana\, capturing in each song the rhythmic pocket Laws is known for cr
 eating.” -  Coyote Music Review 2024\n\n“...His lyrics simply tell fir
 st-person stories from his own life. Nothing fancy\, he's not writing to i
 mpress--he pours himself\, as is\, into each phrase and melody.”- Rebecc
 a Roudman- Dirty Cello Radio Hour KRCB Radio 104.9 FM\n\n“A.M. Sessions 
 is worth your while.” - Wiley Koepp- Texas Drummer
LOCATION:The Porch Kitchen
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/109114546?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://montgomeryvillageca.com/event/annual-tree-lighting-celebration/", "Press Democrat": "https://montgomeryvillageca.com/event/annual-tree-lighting-celebration/", "Visit Santa Rosa": "https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/annual-tree-lighting-celebration/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://montgomeryvillageca.com/event/annual-tree-lighting-celebration/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Annual Tree Lighting Celebration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T190000
UID:261111uJMocrzj2kS41VCO7AcxTA
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to kick off the holiday season with a magical tree l
 ighting experience.\n\nJoin us for our second Annual Tree Lighting Celebra
 tion in The Courtyard near Monti’s and Salt & Straw from 5pm-7pm!\n\nKic
 k off the holiday season with an evening full of festive fun for the whole
  family as we gather for our first annual tree lighting celebration at Mon
 tgomery Village.\n\nFree and open to the community — come celebrate the 
 season with us! Register here.\n\nEnjoy a festive evening filled with holi
 day music\, creative activities\, and a special appearance by Santa and Mr
 s. Claus. Admission is free\, with seasonal fun for the whole family:\n\n-
  Live holiday music and carolers\, plus a family-friendly holiday singalon
 g at 6:45 p.m.\n\n- Complimentary hot cocoa\n\n- Churros and cookies avail
 able for purchase\n\n- Complimentary caricature portraits\n\n- Custom wood
 -burned gift tags\n\n- Make-your-own mini snowmen and jingle bell wreath o
 rnaments\n\n- Write your letters to Santa\, delivered through the official
  Montgomery Village Santa Mail mailbox\n\n- A special visit from Santa and
  Mrs. Claus\n\nMake the evening a little sweeter with a stop at Salt & Str
 aw. During the event\, enjoy a complimentary scoop with the purchase of a 
 scoop\, available November 28\, 2026\, from 5–7 p.m.
LOCATION:Montgomery Village - Courtyard
URL:https://montgomeryvillageca.com/event/annual-tree-lighting-celebration
 /
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat, Visit Santa Rosa
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings", "Press Democrat": "https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Bright Nights at Cuvaison
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T190000
UID:2611153jua4RC9lkiKQTuzRqkwrA
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the magic of the holiday season with Bright Nights\,
  an evening wine tasting experience set against one of Cuvaison’s most e
 nchanting backdrops: rows and rows of estate vineyards illuminated with tw
 inkling lights.\n\nOffered Friday\, Saturday\, and Sunday evenings from No
 vember 27 through January 3\, Bright Nights invites you to experience the 
 beauty of wine country after dark as the vineyard comes alive with a warm 
 holiday glow. From 5:00pm to 7:00pm\, settle in for a cozy seasonal tastin
 g featuring a selection of Cuvaison wines served with seasonal cheese and 
 charcuterie pairing.\n\nWhether you’re gathering with friends\, celebrat
 ing the season\, or creating a new holiday tradition\, Bright Nights offer
 s a festive and memorable way to enjoy the estate.\n\nExperience Highlight
 s:\n\n·         Rows of estate vineyards illuminated with twinkli
 ng holiday lights\n\n·         Curated wine and cheese pairings\n
 \n·         Festive evening tasting from 5:00pm to 7:00pm\n\n· 
         A magical seasonal setting for friends and holiday gatherin
 gs\n\nThis special tasting experience is offered Fridays\, Saturdays and S
 undays from November 27 through January 3\, with reservations beginning at
  5:00\, 5:15\, and 5:30pm. Please include all guests in your reservation.\
 n\nCuvaison and Brandlin Estate members receive preferred pricing and will
  see a $35 discount for up to 4 guests applied at checkout. Please use the
  email address where you receive membership updates in order for your disc
 ount to apply.\n\nCuvaison kindly asks that all guests be 21 years of age 
 or older to enjoy this experience (unless otherwise noted for special fami
 ly friendly dates). The patio is closed during Bright Nights\, so Cuvaison
  is not able to accommodate pets.\n\nImportant Dates:\n\nThursday\, Novemb
 er 12 – Industry Event\n\nSaturday\, November 15 – Member Pick-up Even
 t + Holiday Shopping\n\nFriday\, November 27 – Bright Nights Launch + Bl
 ack Friday Specials\n\nThursday\, December 3 – Bright Nights Workshop ev
 ent\n\nSunday\, December 13 – Bright Nights Family Night (includes milk 
 + cookie pairing for kids\, and a holiday activity). This evening may also
  include a photographer offering Holiday Family portraits.\n\nSunday\, Dec
 ember 27 – Bright Nights Family Night (includes milk + cookie pairing fo
 r kids\, and a holiday activity). This evening may also include a photogra
 pher offering Holiday Family portraits.
LOCATION:Cuvaison Estate Tasting Room
URL:https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings 
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
