SUMMARY:Member Mornings
DESCRIPTION:We LOVE our members! On Sunday and Monday mornings members get exclusive access to the Museum for the first hour! \n\n\n\nAll Children’s Museum members enjoy these benefits:  \n\n\n\n\nFree admission during regular\, open days\n\n\n\nExclusive entrance to the museum during our Sunday Member Mornings \n\n\n\n$2.00 discounts on each admission for up to six additional guests \n\n\n\nDiscounted rates on Gift Corner purchases\, Private Playdates\, birthday parties\, and admission to select events \n\n\n\n$1.00 discounts on each admission for up to four persons to the Schulz Museum and Snoopy’s Home Ice Arena \n\n\n\n\nInterested in becoming a member? Check out our affordable Membership Levels here.
URL:https://www.cmosc.org/event/member-mornings-6/2026-11-29/
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://www.cmosc.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/the_power_of_play_at_the_childrens_museum-37.webp
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.goldengatemarinart.org/copy-of-contact"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Discovering Women Poets\, a Poetry Competition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T235900
UID:2611216tX6ncGjpEmxxRdFYWJ7-g
DESCRIPTION:The National League of American Pen Women (NLAPW) and the Gold
 en Gate-Marin Branch are launching a poetry competition for women over 18 
 years of age who are not currently members of the NLAPW. This regional and
  national competition will be run at the Branch level in the semi-finalist
  phase. Local winners are automatically entered into the League’s Nation
 al competition.\n\nWinners at the Branch level will receive $35 and have t
 heir entry published in the Branch newsletter. They will also be invited t
 o present their poetry in person or by Zoom.\n\nBranch winners become semi
 -finalists in the National competition\, which will award $100 to three wi
 nners. National winners will have their work and a short bio published in 
 The Pen Woman\, a national magazine. All semi-finalists will be listed in 
 the magazine.\n\nUp to three poems may be submitted for one entry fee of $
 15. Each poem should be no longer than 40 lines. There are no restrictions
  on topics or poem’s structure. Entries must be received by January 25\,
  2027.\n\nDownload Entry Form at our website: https://www.goldengatemarina
 rt.org/copy-of-contact
LOCATION:https://www.goldengatemarinart.org/
URL:https://www.goldengatemarinart.org/copy-of-contact
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Press Democrat": "https://www.thesearanchlodge.com/programming/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Press Democrat": "https://www.thesearanchlodge.com/programming/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:pressdemocrat
SUMMARY:Mushroom Foraging
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T120000
UID:261114qiMZM3BYHUKicZ7aL_ZZyg
DESCRIPTION:Wild mushroom season has arrived on the Sonoma Coast\, where m
 isty forests and coastal meadows nurture a dazzling diversity of fungi for
  curious foragers and culinary enthusiasts alike.\n\nJoin Ty the Fungi\, a
  seasoned local forager with nearly 15 years of experience\, and learn how
  to find\, identify\, and responsibly harvest wild mushrooms—from prized
  edibles to those best left untouched. Discover the principles of ethical 
 foraging and deepen your connection to the landscape through this immersiv
 e\, hands-on exploration.\n\nMeet at The Lodge’s Fireside Lounge\, and w
 e’ll caravan together to the foraging site.\n\n$160 per person\, $100 (a
 ges 10-16). Space is limited. This adventure is recommended for participan
 ts with moderate to advanced hiking experience.
LOCATION:The Sea Ranch Lodge 
URL:https://www.thesearanchlodge.com/programming/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
