X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:A Taste of Italy at Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T170000
UID:260430F51ZeVxRhUOSYf5QVS5O-A
DESCRIPTION:For wine drinkers eager to experience world-class wines made i
 n California from Italian varieties\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
  is a must during any trip to Sonoma County. Located just off the plaza in
  the charming town of Healdsburg near famed restaurants\, boutiques and ga
 lleries\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room is a destination that invit
 es discovery. Founded by the acclaimed team that guides renowned Pinot Noi
 r and Chardonnay producer Rhys Vineyards\, Centennial Mountain was establi
 shed to explore Italian grape varieties grown on its acclaimed Centennial 
 Mountain Vineyard in the rugged mountains of Northern Sonoma County.\n\nTh
 e Centennial Mountain Vineyard Tasting features the winery’s coveted Neb
 biolo\, and the pioneering Carricante and Nerello Mascalese wines\, among 
 others. To showcase how beautifully the wines pair with food\, the winery 
 also offers a delicious Wine and Sushi Pairing from nearby Asahi Sushi\, o
 ne of Healdsburg’s most popular dining destinations.\n\nGuests can also 
 enhance their tasting experience with a curated salumi board from Journeym
 an Meat Company. This generous accompaniment features six house-made salum
 i\, crostini\, cornichons\, olives\, and a selection of local cheese that 
 serves 2 to 5 guests.
LOCATION:Centennial Mountain Tasting Room 
URL:https://cmvineyard.com/visit/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.upstairsartgallery.net", "Press Democrat": "http://www.upstairsartgallery.net"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.upstairsartgallery.net"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Winter Magic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T180000
UID:261116FNJFpm-NNEK5RtD2xqL6Aw
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  11/15/26\n\n**DECEMBER EXHIBIT: 
 WINTER MAGIC**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  November 23– December 27\, 2026\n\n**
 RECEPTION/HOLIDAY OPEN HOUSE: DECEMBER 5\, 2026\, 11am to 6pm: Join in to 
 meet the artists and cheer the season\, the show and enjoy holiday goodies
 . As part of the festivities\, we will host our monthly free drawing for a
 n artwork by Ron Sumner.  The Gallery is pleased to participate again thi
 s year in the Healdsburg Chamber’s Holiday Sip & Shop – for more infor
 mation: 2026 Healdsburg Holiday Sip & Shop\, Eventbrite.com.**\n\nSonoma C
 ounty artists\, **Willow LaLand\, Phyllis Rapp\, Linda Loveland Reid\, Lau
 ra Roney\, Luba Stolper\, Ron Sumner\, Jo Tobin-Charleston\, Carolyn Wilso
 n and Gen Zorich** present **Winter Magic\,** a mix of unique artistic exp
 ressions creating a magical welcome to the 2026 holiday season.  Starting
  with nature’s magic -the colorful painterly skies at dawn and dusk – 
 LaLand’s “Boston Harbor” at sunrise engenders warm feelings of hope 
 as does Roney’s “Dancing in the Snow” in the waning rays of daylight
 .  Stolper weaves a spell with “Whispering Elegance\,” objects so rea
 l – the lace\, the cherries\, the vase- the viewer is drawn in awe.  Wi
 lson’s “New Beginnings” draws the viewer’s eye with lively colorfu
 l flowers that seem to dance for joy.  Artists Rapp and Sumner turn to ou
 r feline and feathered friends for inspiration:  in Rapp’s “Emerald E
 ye\,” the kitty captivates us with a mesmerizing gaze and Sumner’s “
 Snowy Owl” looks out from its perch in a moonlit snowy glen.   From ou
 r abstract artists\, Reid lights our spirit with “Green for Joy” and Z
 orich’s “Layers and Red Rock\, “compelling in texture with splashes 
 of random color shapes. To enable us to cast one’s own spell\, Tobin-Cha
 rleston’s sparkle/colored-themed crystal pendant sets are the perfect ti
 cket.\n\nAll member artists are showing many smaller works throughout the 
 Gallery\, ideal for gifting.\n\nFor the Holiday Season our **Staircase Sho
 wcase** features many different hand-crafted 3D artist offerings. Ceramic 
 artists Kathy Brown\, Joann Cassady\, Ed Price\, Karen Norton and Steve Sa
 nders offer a variety of vases\, platters\, and bowls.  Our glass artists
 \, Brian & Nancy Roberts\, Melissa McCann and Tim Montesouti present gorge
 ous fused glass art\, decorative boxes\, and tree ornaments. Plus\, we hav
 e horsehair bowls and decorated gourds by Susan Miron and wooden bird scul
 ptures presented by Amber Biocca. And\, as always\, there is jewelry throu
 ghout the gallery. You can find the perfect earrings\, necklace\, pendant 
 or bracelet from our local jewelers: Galley-member Jo Tobin-Charleston\, A
 aron Poovey\, Laura Buckner\, Melissa McCann\, Patricia Reilly\, Hamida Ju
 dith Dides\, Elaine Greene\, Heyoka Merrifield\, and JoAnna Noble.\n\n**JO
 IN US for ARTNITE HEALDSBURG\, THURSDAY\, DECEMBER 3  5:00 – 7:00 pm** 
 : Artnite Healdsburg is a community event celebrating art and creativity w
 ith more than 20 galleries participating\, along with select restaurants\,
  bars and boutiques. \n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Heald
 sburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm\; extended ho
 liday hours: Open Fri & Sat 10am – 7pm through December 23rd\; closed De
 cember 25.    **www.upstairsartgallery.net** \n\nFor further informatio
 n: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-
 1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.fvaa-arts.org/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:FSVAA 63rd Annual Nor-Cal Regional Juried Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T180000
UID:261113F_nXNqKUP02NAVCsc418Fw
DESCRIPTION:2026 Juried Art Exhibit: Celebrating Northern California’s A
 rtistic Excellence!\n\nFSVAA proudly presents the 63rd Annual Nor-Cal Regi
 onal Juried Art Show at the Solano Town Center Gallery – show opening is
  Friday\, Nov 13. Gallery Hours are Wed thru Sun\, 11am–6pm.\n\n The th
 ree jurors\, Ferdinanda Florence\, Nadja Fitchhorn\, and Vickie Marchand h
 ave spoken and made their selections!\n\nWe received 200 art entries from 
 67 talented artists representing 15 different cities throughout Northern C
 alifornia\, making this an exciting and impressive year for our Juried Art
  Show.\n\nIt was wonderful to see so many artists arrive with their treasu
 red works of art\, eager to have them reviewed and considered by our three
  distinguished jurors.\n\nAfter careful deliberation\, the jurors selected
  97 outstanding works of art to be included in this year's Juried Art Show
 !\n\nCongratulations to all the artists whose work was selected\, and than
 k you to everyone who participated and helped make this year's show such a
  success.\n\nEXHIBIT INFORMATION \\(Save the Dates\\):\n\n• Art Show Rec
 eption /Awards Gala: Saturday\, Dec 5\, 2026\, 3–5pm\n\n• Reception /P
 oetry Reading: Saturday\, Dec 19\, 2026\, 3–5pm\n\n• Juror's Talk: Sun
 day\, Jan 3\, 2027\, 1–3pm at the Solano Town Center Gallery  – Come 
 hear our Jurors speak! Join us as they share their insights into the selec
 tion process\, discuss what goes into choosing artwork for a juried exhibi
 tion\, and offer a glimpse into their experience. As always\, there will b
 e time for a Q&A\, so bring your questions!
LOCATION:Solano Town Center Gallery
URL:https://www.fvaa-arts.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
