BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.tinyurl.com/Patron-Saints-form", "Press Democrat": "http://www.tinyurl.com/Patron-Saints-form"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.tinyurl.com/Patron-Saints-form"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Patron Saints of Influence Fall Reading + Open Mic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T180000
UID:261031SNAVOb4og0KeSe1XIUq7_w
DESCRIPTION:The next Patron Saints literary reading & open mic will pay ho
 mage to mother of science fiction Mary Shelley with featured readings by L
 auren C. Johnson\, Shawna Swetech\, and Wendy M. Thompson.\n\nAs always\, 
 you are welcome to share your own written work in 5 minutes or less during
  the open mic. All words are welcome as long as they're not hateful or AI-
 generated.\n\nAbout the featured readers:\n\nLauren C. Johnson attributes 
 her upbringing in Florida–America’s weirdest state–to her interest i
 n the ecological and surreal. She's the interviews editor for The Racket J
 ournal\, where she champions experimental literature\, and is a co-founder
  and editor of Club Chicxulub\, a speculative fiction journal and reading 
 series that amplifies emerging authors. She also co-hosts Babylon Salon\, 
 one of the longest-running reading series in the Bay Area. Her short stori
 es\, interviews\, and essays have appeared in numerous journals\, includin
 g The Rumpus and Orion Magazine online. The West Façade is her debut nove
 l. Find out more at **www.laurencjohnson.com.**\n\nShawna L. Swetech is a
  retired hospital nurse\, poet\, artist and integrative health practitione
 r. Her poetry appears in Rattle\, The Healing Muse\, Pulse\, the American 
 Journal of Nursing and other journals and anthologies. Her work ranges fro
 m the personal to the universal\, the body to the body politic\, drawing f
 rom the deep wells of human nature and the natural world. Shawna is a co-h
 ost for the monthly reading series\, Rivertown Poets. She is the author of
  a newly-released poetry collection based on her 35 year career as a regis
 tered nurse\, entitled “Standing in Their Fire.” (Kelsay Books\, 2026)
  **www.ShawnaSwetech.com**\n\nWendy M. Thompson is a poet\, writer\, and 
 scholar who hails from Oakland\, California. Her debut poetry collection B
 lack California Gold (Bucknell University Press\, 2025) maps out life in t
 he Bay Area during the 1980s and 1990s and was a finalist for the 2025 Mar
 tin Cruz Smith Award: Emerging Diverse Voices prize. She has a forthcoming
  book\, Chasing the Sun: Staging Black Life\, Belonging\, and Displacement
  in California’s Bay Area (University of Washington Press\, 2027)\, that
  looks at the cultural and performative worlds of black migrants and their
  descendants who staged mobility\, home\, and refusal during Second Great 
 Migration into the contemporary era. She is an Associate Professor of Afri
 can American Studies at San José State University.
LOCATION:Shady Oak Barrel House
URL:http://www.tinyurl.com/Patron-Saints-form
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.northbayoa.org/", "Press Democrat": "https://www.northbayoa.org/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.northbayoa.org/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Overeaters Anonymous (OA) Newcomer Meeting in Santa Rosa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T170000
UID:260212HHa-Z_8mokGbhdqwKNkCJQ
DESCRIPTION:**Is Food a Problem for You? You Are Not Alone.**\n\nOvereater
 s Anonymous (OA) is a fellowship of people who support each other in recov
 ering from compulsive eating and food behaviors. If you feel you have a pr
 oblem with food\, OA welcomes you—no matter what your background\, belie
 fs\, or eating habits.\n\nWe hold an in-person newcomer meeting on **Sunda
 ys from 4:00 – 5:00 PM** **at Christ Church United Methodist\, 1717 Yulu
 pa Ave.\, Room #4\, Santa Rosa**. Contact: Abigail (707) 293-5888. You may
  view all North Bay OA in-person and online meetings at https://www.northb
 ayoa.org/meetings.html .\n\nIn OA\, members experience **spiritual\, emoti
 onal\, and physical recovery** by practicing the **Twelve Steps** and livi
 ng by their spiritual principles—one day at a time.\n\nOA is **not** a d
 iet club or calorie-counting program.\n\nMembers have different plans of e
 ating.\n\nOA does **not** endorse any specific food plan.\n\nIf food is ca
 using problems in your life\, you don’t have to struggle alone. Recovery
  is possible\, and help is available.\n\n**Visit:** https://www.northbayoa
 .org/\n\n**Find a meeting:** https://www.northbayoa.org/meetings.html
LOCATION:Christ Church United Methodist
URL:https://www.northbayoa.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings", "Press Democrat": "https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Bright Nights at Cuvaison
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T190000
UID:261115P2MfT9dY-Uu8NQX72xrMUg
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the magic of the holiday season with Bright Nights\,
  an evening wine tasting experience set against one of Cuvaison’s most e
 nchanting backdrops: rows and rows of estate vineyards illuminated with tw
 inkling lights.\n\nOffered Friday\, Saturday\, and Sunday evenings from No
 vember 27 through January 3\, Bright Nights invites you to experience the 
 beauty of wine country after dark as the vineyard comes alive with a warm 
 holiday glow. From 5:00pm to 7:00pm\, settle in for a cozy seasonal tastin
 g featuring a selection of Cuvaison wines served with seasonal cheese and 
 charcuterie pairing.\n\nWhether you’re gathering with friends\, celebrat
 ing the season\, or creating a new holiday tradition\, Bright Nights offer
 s a festive and memorable way to enjoy the estate.\n\nExperience Highlight
 s:\n\n·         Rows of estate vineyards illuminated with twinkli
 ng holiday lights\n\n·         Curated wine and cheese pairings\n
 \n·         Festive evening tasting from 5:00pm to 7:00pm\n\n· 
         A magical seasonal setting for friends and holiday gatherin
 gs\n\nThis special tasting experience is offered Fridays\, Saturdays and S
 undays from November 27 through January 3\, with reservations beginning at
  5:00\, 5:15\, and 5:30pm. Please include all guests in your reservation.\
 n\nCuvaison and Brandlin Estate members receive preferred pricing and will
  see a $35 discount for up to 4 guests applied at checkout. Please use the
  email address where you receive membership updates in order for your disc
 ount to apply.\n\nCuvaison kindly asks that all guests be 21 years of age 
 or older to enjoy this experience (unless otherwise noted for special fami
 ly friendly dates). The patio is closed during Bright Nights\, so Cuvaison
  is not able to accommodate pets.\n\nImportant Dates:\n\nThursday\, Novemb
 er 12 – Industry Event\n\nSaturday\, November 15 – Member Pick-up Even
 t + Holiday Shopping\n\nFriday\, November 27 – Bright Nights Launch + Bl
 ack Friday Specials\n\nThursday\, December 3 – Bright Nights Workshop ev
 ent\n\nSunday\, December 13 – Bright Nights Family Night (includes milk 
 + cookie pairing for kids\, and a holiday activity). This evening may also
  include a photographer offering Holiday Family portraits.\n\nSunday\, Dec
 ember 27 – Bright Nights Family Night (includes milk + cookie pairing fo
 r kids\, and a holiday activity). This evening may also include a photogra
 pher offering Holiday Family portraits.
