 ions and bibliographies\, and offers note-taking\, outlining\, and paper-w
 riting features\, including the capability to create papers via GoogleDocs
 .<br />Workshop Details: Extra Credit available!<br />You will learn how t
 o sign up for an account with NoodleTools. We will also provide examples t
 o show how to create citations\, create a bibliography and check for error
 s. There will be time to ask questions at the end of the overview bring yo
 ur sources along. Join us for a workshop and learn how to cite your source
 s right!<br />Extra Credit: As students\, you have the option to submit yo
 ur instructor and course name when you register if you would like us to no
 tify your instructor that you have attended the workshop for extra credit.
  Or\, you can work with your instructor on an alternative way to provide e
 vidence of your attendance.<br />Registration: (click "Begin Registration"
  button below)<br />This workshop does not require registration. However\,
  registering will guarantee admittance to this in-person workshop. Please 
 arrive promptly.<br />Workshop Location: Santa Rosa Campus\, Doyle Library
 \, Room 4327. See map for directions to Doyle Library.<br />The workshop w
 ill open 5 minutes prior to the start time.<br />Attendees are asked to ab
 ide by SRJC student conduct policy.<br />Have questions? Chat with an SRJC
