BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://secure.qgiv.com/for/jcwzbq/event/coronacapricreek/", "Press Democrat": "https://secure.qgiv.com/for/jcwzbq/event/coronacapricreek/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://secure.qgiv.com/for/jcwzbq/event/coronacapricreek/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Reimagining the Rain in Corona/Capri Creek
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261203T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261203T193000
UID:261116Qp8hZ2qa3UGticeb47rAcQ
DESCRIPTION:Si hablas español\, habrá un intérprete en este evento. Ind
 ícanoslo en el último paso al inscribirte en el evento.\n\nWhat would it
  look like if our neighborhoods were designed to work with and welcome wat
 er instead of sending it away?\n\nAs a part of our Harvest the Rain Pilot 
 Program\, Daily Acts is inviting Petaluma community members who live near
  or are frequent visitors in the Corona/Capri Creek area to REIMAGINE TH
 E RAIN by attending an interactive\, neighborhood-based community input se
 ssion.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_
 \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\
 _\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\
 nJoin this Community Input Session to:\n\n-Help us understand your experie
 nce with stormwater\n\n-Learn from local experts in our community\n\n-Conn
 ect with your neighbors over FREE dinner\n\n-Provide feedback on DIY rain 
 garden and curb cut templates\n\n-Enter a gift card drawing for local bus
 inesses like Petaluma Coffee & Tea\, Refill Mercantile and The Seed Bank!\
 n\nDuring the session\, we'll discuss how we can work with rainwater to bu
 ild resilient neighborhoods. We’ll hear from you to learn where you’ve
  noticed water pooling in your neighborhood\, and explore whether those pl
 aces are creating challenges\, or if they could be the beginning of an opp
 ortunity to work with water in an exciting new way! We will also gather yo
 ur feedback on the rain garden and curb-cut landscape templates we’re de
 veloping.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_
 \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\
 _\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_
 \n\nlf you live near or frequent Corona/Capri Creek\, we want to hear fro
 m you!\n\nCome share your observations\, what you’d like to see in your 
 neighborhood\, and any questions\, excitement or concerns you may have abo
 ut this pilot program. We hope to see you there!\n\nQuestions? Please ema
 il moreinfo@dailyacts.org or call \\(707\\) 200-8364
LOCATION:Petaluma Community Center (Lucchesi)
URL:https://secure.qgiv.com/for/jcwzbq/event/coronacapricreek/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
