BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.goldengatemarinart.org/copy-of-contact"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Discovering Women Poets\, a Poetry Competition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T235900
UID:261121cezsacY_dkGcg9BuThruDQ
DESCRIPTION:The National League of American Pen Women (NLAPW) and the Gold
 en Gate-Marin Branch are launching a poetry competition for women over 18 
 years of age who are not currently members of the NLAPW. This regional and
  national competition will be run at the Branch level in the semi-finalist
  phase. Local winners are automatically entered into the League’s Nation
 al competition.\n\nWinners at the Branch level will receive $35 and have t
 heir entry published in the Branch newsletter. They will also be invited t
 o present their poetry in person or by Zoom.\n\nBranch winners become semi
 -finalists in the National competition\, which will award $100 to three wi
 nners. National winners will have their work and a short bio published in 
 The Pen Woman\, a national magazine. All semi-finalists will be listed in 
 the magazine.\n\nUp to three poems may be submitted for one entry fee of $
 15. Each poem should be no longer than 40 lines. There are no restrictions
  on topics or poem’s structure. Entries must be received by January 25\,
  2027.\n\nDownload Entry Form at our website: https://www.goldengatemarina
 rt.org/copy-of-contact
LOCATION:https://www.goldengatemarinart.org/
URL:https://www.goldengatemarinart.org/copy-of-contact
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sec.regfox.com/2026taichi", "Press Democrat": "https://sec.regfox.com/2026taichi", "Visit Santa Rosa": "https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/park-rx-tai-chi-flow-winter-2026/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sec.regfox.com/2026taichi"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Park Rx—Tai Chi Flow
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T100000
UID:261021mHfyKIgWykW6-RBhvmWuTQ
DESCRIPTION:Embrace the tranquility of winter Sunday mornings at Sugarloaf
  as our experienced instructor\, Diana Latorre\, guides you in the ancient
  practice of Tai Chi every first and third Sunday of the month. This gentl
 e holistic wellness practice is perfect for beginners and those with limit
 ed mobility\, as the practice can be done seated. Not recommended for chil
 dren under 16 years old.\n\nTickets are $15 or free with a September 2026 
 or newer Park Rx from a Sonoma County Medical Provider. Click here for Par
 k Rx information. To sign up with a Park Rx\, please email the signed Rx f
 orm to alma@sonomaecologycenter.org. Please have your Rx available at the 
 time of sign-up\, as the number of Park Rx tickets is limited and you will
  be asked to turn in a copy at the time of registration. Wear layers\, com
 fortable footwear\, bring water\, sun protection\, and if desired\, a snac
 k or a picnic to enjoy after the event. Parking fees apply. Heavy rains ca
 ncel.
