X-SOURCE-ID:pressdemocrat
SUMMARY:Tending the Spark: InterChurch Food Pantry Benefit Concert
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T180000
UID:261118uZXtoaIEtUCvheFGhD-Htg
DESCRIPTION:"Tending the Spark" is a heartfelt evening of inspirational si
 nging presented by Joyful Noise! Gospel Singers featuring the powerful voi
 ces and musicianship of consummate performers Melanie DeMore\, BenjaSoul (
 Benja Mertz)\, and Francisco Herrera. Audience participation is encouraged
 \, and Harmonia Community Choir (Sebastopol Center for the Arts’ residen
 t choir) led by John Maas will also sing.\n\nFood scarcity is a problem fo
 r many of our Sebastopol area neighbors. The first two benefit concerts ra
 ised just under $12\,000 for the Food Pantry\, giving a meaningful infusio
 n of “green energy” to this vital resource.\n\nThis is the third annua
 l fundraiser concert for the Interchurch Food Pantry.  Suggested donation
  of $20 (cash or check) at the door\, no one turned away. 100% of donation
 s will go to support the Food Pantry. \n\nThe venue is the beautiful Comm
 unity Church of Sebastopol\, 1000 Gravenstein Hwy N\, Sebastopol. (Please 
 arrive early to assure your seat\, as it has been full every year!)
LOCATION:Community Church of Sebastopol
URL:https://www.joyfulnoisegospelsingers.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
