BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://secure.qgiv.com/for/jcwzbq/event/washingtoncreek/", "Press Democrat": "https://secure.qgiv.com/for/jcwzbq/event/washingtoncreek/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://secure.qgiv.com/for/jcwzbq/event/washingtoncreek/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Reimagining the Rain in Washington Creek
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261210T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261210T193000
UID:261116r-dD4_IsEUyARoAhgm6O9A
DESCRIPTION:Si hablas español\, habrá un intérprete en este evento. Ind
 ícanoslo en el último paso al inscribirte en el evento.\n\nWhat would it
  look like if our neighborhoods were designed to work with and welcome wat
 er instead of sending it away?\n\nAs a part of our Harvest the Rain Pilot 
 Program\, Daily Acts is inviting Petaluma community members who live near
  or are frequent visitors in the Washington Creek area to REIMAGINE THE 
 RAIN by attending an interactive\, neighborhood-based community input sess
 ion.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_
 \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\
 _\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_
 \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nJoin this Community Input Session 
 to:\n\n-Help us understand your experience with stormwater\n\n-Learn from 
 local experts in our community\n\n-Connect with your neighbors over FREE d
 inner\n\n-Provide feedback on DIY rain garden and curb cut templates\n\n-E
 nter a gift card drawing for local businesses like Petaluma Coffee & Tea\
 , Caffeine Inc.\, Refill Mercantile and The Seed Bank!\n\nDuring the sessi
 on\, we'll discuss how we can work with rainwater to build resilient neigh
 borhoods. We’ll hear from you to learn where you’ve noticed water pool
 ing in your neighborhood\, and explore whether those places are creating c
 hallenges\, or if they could be the beginning of an opportunity to work wi
 th water in an exciting new way! We will also gather your feedback on the 
 rain garden and curb-cut landscape templates we’re developing. \n\n\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_
 \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\
 _\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\
 \_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_
 \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nlf you live near or frequent Washington
  Creek\, we want to hear from you!\n\nCome share your observations\, what 
 you’d like to see in your neighborhood\, and any questions\, excitement 
 or concerns you may have about this pilot program. We hope to see you ther
 e!\n\nQuestions? Please email moreinfo@dailyacts.org or call \\(707\\) 20
 0-8364
LOCATION:Petaluma Community Center (Lucchesi)
URL:https://secure.qgiv.com/for/jcwzbq/event/washingtoncreek/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
