SUMMARY:The Story Shuffle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T210000
UID:261118zqLUgYoXkEuL8ImDBZ-2NA
DESCRIPTION:The Story Shuffle - The Truth\, The Half Truth and Nothing Lik
 e The Truth!\n\nJoin us for storytelling in Novato! We’ll have featured 
 storytellers and then an Open Mic part of the show\, featuring two options
 : you can either throw your name in the hat to tell a 5-minute story or a 
 1-minute story in our Story Sprint lighting round. No theme\, just bring y
 our best story. Sign up at the door. Come out for a night of live\, friend
 ly and fun storytelling in a cozy\, comfortable venue that is just right f
 or an evening of great tales. Newcomers to storytelling very welcome. We
 ’d love to see you there. PLUS we will celebrate the Season with some fe
 stive food - a few appetizers from England and America.
LOCATION:Courtyard by Marriott
URL:http://www.sixfeetapartproductions.com/shuffle.php
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.occidentalchoir.org/concerts", "Visit Santa Rosa": "https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/when-i-rise-up-choral-series-in-santa-rosa/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.occidentalchoir.org/concerts"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:When I Rise Up - Choral Series
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T210000
UID:261116mHnuu-H_CkGC-0LNtO1tzg
DESCRIPTION:The Occidental Community Choir puts on live concerts featuring
  an eclectic mix of locally composed music\, classical and contemporary ch
 oral pieces\, poetry\, and spoken word from our community in the redwoods 
 of Northern California.\n\nThis season\, "When I Rise Up\," will remind us
  that hope is not passive\, justice is not someone else's work\, and the f
 uture is something that we create together. We'll explore songs of joy\, h
 ope\, resilience\, justice\, and protest. Some of our programming will cha
 llenge us to confront difficult truths and some of it will remind us that 
 even in times of division\, compassion\, courage\, and community can light
  the way forward.\n\nWe don't answer those questions all at once. We endea
 vor to answer it by the choices we make\, by the people we stand beside\, 
 and by the hope we refuse to surrender.\n\nJoin the Occidental Community C
 hoir this winter for an evening of music that aims to bring a little more 
 light into this world.
LOCATION:Glaser Center
URL:https://www.occidentalchoir.org/concerts
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Visit Santa Rosa
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Occidental Center for the Arts": "https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/nina-gerber-keith-greeninger", "North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.facebook.com/events/28948963218095260/", "Creative Sonoma": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/nina-gerber-keith-greeninger/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Occidental Center for the Arts": "https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/nina-gerber-keith-greeninger"}
X-SOURCE-ID:occidental_arts
SUMMARY:Nina Gerber & Keith Greeninger
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T213000
UID:6a908a63fe78242bc9fe161f@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:Award winning singer/songwriter and legendary guitarist join f
 orces for special performance!\nAward winning singer/songwriter Keith Gree
 ninger and legendary guitarist Nina Gerber join forces for a powerful nigh
 t of music\, song and community celebration. Both artists share deep roots
  in the rich California music scene and are well know for their dynamic\, 
 improvisational performances and collaborations.\nDon't miss this special 
 performance! Tickets are $35 General Admission\, $30 for OCA members. We e
 xpect this show to sell out so get your tickets early!\nGet Tickets\nGuita
 rist\nNina Gerber\nstarted her music career playing along side of the icon
 ic singer songwriter Kate Wolf. She has since gone on to establish herself
  as one of the finest guitarists on the planet performing and recording wi
 th some of the genre’s finest songwriters including Nanci Griffith\, Kar
 la Bonoff\, Greg Brown\, Eliza Gilkyson\, Laurie Lewis and Chris Webster j
 ust to name a few.\nKeith Greeninger\nis a compelling singer/songwriter an
 d performer whose songs have won top honors at such prestigious music fest
 ivals as the Telluride Bluegrass Festival and the Kerrville Folk Festival.
  A seasoned troubador who paints intricate portraits of the human conditio
 n with powerful melodic images\, deep engaging guitar rhythms and compelli
 ng\, heart-wrenching vocals\, his songs cut an honest\, hard worn path to 
 places of simple truth about good people holding on to hope and instinct i
 n a world that often tries to strip these things away.
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal\, CA 95465
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/nina-gerber
 -keith-greeninger
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts, Creative Sonoma, North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
