BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/jumpstart-your-art/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Jumpstart Your Art
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261214T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261214T160000
UID:260629iTDcLxVpe0O_gjhC8UEkHQ
DESCRIPTION:Every person experiences an ebb and flow to the tides of their
  creativity. We will share space together to design\, exchange ideas\, and
  hold ourselves accountable to our unique interests! The first portion of 
 our time together will involve a check-in discussion of ‘what is'\, lead
 ing into ‘what could be'. The talk will be facilitated by Erin Partridge
 \, an art therapist with a long history of supporting people in reengaging
  with creativity. After our initial talk\, we will have some time to indiv
 idually focus on our creative practices in the space of the gallery. Befor
 e we close\, we will share anything that came up in the process. Bring you
 r ideas\, a project\, and an interest in creative community. Please be min
 dful of what you choose to show up with-something quiet\, easy to clean up
 \, and non-disruptive to your fellow creatives. Not sure where to begin? S
 ome basic materials are available\, thanks to a donation from  Blick Art M
 aterials . Open for all ages-youth under 12 with an adult chaperone please
 ! Mondays\, 1-4 PM Facilitator: Erin Partridge
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/jumpstart-your-art/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.gvrd.org/wilson-park-community-outreach-meetings"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Vallejo Community Center
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261214T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261214T153000
UID:261116_6_eX4CKGUGh6FD_Fa_mGg
DESCRIPTION:The City of Vallejo\, in partnership with the Greater Vallejo 
 Recreation District \\(GVRD\\)\, invites residents\, families\, and commun
 ity partners to help shape the future of Wilson Park!\n\nThe City is pursu
 ing funding through California's Statewide Park Development Grant Program 
 \\(Proposition 4\\) to support potential renovations and improvements to W
 ilson Park.\n\nThis is an exciting opportunity to explore ways to create a
  safer\, more welcoming\, accessible\, and vibrant neighborhood park for e
 veryone to enjoy.\n\nWhat Would You Like to See at Wilson Park? Your ideas
  can help identify potential park improvements\, including:\n\nNew recreat
 ional amenities and play features\n\nSafer\, more accessible spaces for al
 l ages and abilities\n\nLandscaping\, shade\, and beautification\n\nFamily
 -friendly gathering and relaxation areas\n\nOpportunities for recreation\,
  wellness\, and neighborhood connections\n\nNo final renovation plan has b
 een selected. Community input will help guide the proposed improvements.
LOCATION:GVRD Board Room
URL:https://www.gvrd.org/wilson-park-community-outreach-meetings
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
