X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_c_rilc5rtgatnr4oln08fo9p5k30
SUMMARY:Sips and Stars
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T190000
DTSTAMP:20261121T065135Z
UID:6pv7eu9qsf2f0jl74gbsus70t0@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T163000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260429T174738Z
DESCRIPTION:Sips and Stars ~ an evening of fine wine and cosmic wonder.\n\
 nJoin us for a magical night under the stars at the Robert Ferguson Observ
 atory! Our Sips & Stars event blends the beauty of the night sky with the 
 elegance of Sonoma County wine. Enjoy a curated tasting experience hosted 
 by Burtech Family Vineyard\,  while taking in breathtaking views of the c
 osmos through our powerful telescopes.\n\nAs twilight falls\, relax with a
  glass of wine in hand and listen to engaging astronomy talks from our kno
 wledgeable docents. Once darkness settles\, step up to the observatory’s
  telescopes for guided viewing of planets\, star clusters\, and distant ga
 laxies.\n\nWhether you’re a wine lover\, stargazer\, or simply looking f
 or a unique evening out in Sonoma Valley\, Sips & Stars promises an unforg
 ettable experience where earthly pleasures meet celestial beauty.\n\nGuest
 s must be 21 or older to attend and each registration includes two drink t
 ickets. Proceeds support the Robert Ferguson Observatory’s public educat
 ion programs.\n\nSpace is limited - register at rfo.simpletix.com
LAST-MODIFIED:20260429T174738Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Robert Ferguson Observatory
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Press Democrat": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108097057?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:pressdemocrat
SUMMARY:Callie Watts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T170000
UID:261116jT85cMzD0kGM68D02Jfvpw
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:Tasting Notes
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108097057?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
